      "lineNbr": 199,
      "author": {
        "id": 1155599
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-14T11:04:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So, `createSettingsUrl()` returns the canonical path, which usually starts with `/`, i.e. `/settings`, this would correctly re-route to the settings page as expected (see L196), if it wasn\u0027t that this line changes it to `http:///settings`, because it doesn\u0027t start with `http`.\n\nYou\u0027re right to question this though, In trying to be conservative, I didn\u0027t dig deep enough into why we have this line to begin with. It looks like it was questioned when it was introduced too [1] and the suggested fix was never applied.\n\nMaybe this line could go all together replaced by the `getNavigation`.\nLet me do some further digging and I\u0027ll get back to you.\n\n[1] https://gerrit-review.googlesource.com/c/gerrit/+/522821/comment/d1281df4_2365b82e/",
      "parentUuid": "b1693365_47d7cdff",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 199,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 199,
        "endChar": 66
      },
      "revId": "b2b051a22958ddab9e920faf8e93642095ce16d6",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
